# Products and components

Wyrd documentation has two ways in: the job you are trying to do and the
component you are working with. This page is the component map.

## Wyrd core

Wyrd owns the Card contract, registry, lineage, policy, identity, install, and
audit surfaces.

- [Overview](/overview/) — what Wyrd is and what runs today.
- [Concepts](/concepts/) — the Card, Spec, Run, and Observation model.
- [Architecture](/concepts/architecture/) — how the Wyrd products fit together.

## Cards

Cards are the shared declaration format for Wyrd components.

- [Cards overview](/cards/) — envelope, registration boundary, and kind status.
- [Card concept](/concepts/card/) — identity, lifecycle, and references.
- [Declare a card](/how-to/declare/) — author Data, Model, and Prompt cards.
- [Card schemas](/api/schemas/) — generated JSON Schema inventory.

## Skald

Skald owns provider clients, prompt execution, tools, agents, and workflows.

- [Skald overview](/skald/) — its runtime boundary and relationship to Cards.
- [Agent and workflow architecture](/concepts/architecture/) —
  where Skald sits in the Wyrd system.
- [Build an agent](/how-to/build-an-agent/) — create a bounded agent loop.
- [Build a workflow](/how-to/build-a-workflow/) — compose agent invocations.

## Bifrost

Bifrost is Wyrd's analytical warehouse and observability data plane.

- [Bifrost overview](/bifrost/) — how Gate, Scribe, Oracle, and Forge fit together.
- [Quickstart](/bifrost/quickstart/) — emit and query an observation.
- [Architecture](/bifrost/architecture/) — storage, concurrency, and data flow.

## Fathom

[Fathom](/fathom/) is the planned intelligence layer that reads Wyrd's typed
model and turns runtime behavior into evidence. It is not released yet, so its
page explains the relationship without documenting an unavailable workflow.
